Bugfix: Improve resilience of repository v2 upgrade rollback

When an upgrade from repository version 1 to version 2 failed, restic
deleted the configuration file before writing the previous version back.
On backends that replace files atomically, such as the local backend, that
file was still the valid version 1 configuration. If writing it back also
failed, the repository no longer had a configuration file and could not be
opened. Restic now writes the previous configuration back without deleting
the file first on those backends.

